<title>USA: U.S. supply/demand cotton estimates -- USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. supply/demand cotton estimates -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA supply/demand estimates of U.S. cotton (million 480-Lb Bales):</p>
<p>				    1996/97		  1995/96</p>
<p>			   11/01/96  12/01/96   11/01/96   12/01/96</p>
<p>   Beginning Stocks-U    2.61	 2.61	 2.65	2.65</p>
<p>	     Production   18.59	18.19	17.90     17.90</p>
<p>		  Imports    0.50	 0.50	 0.41	0.41</p>
<p>	 Total Supply-F   21.70	21.30	20.96     20.96</p>
<p>	   Domestic Use   11.00	11.00	10.60     10.60</p>
<p>		  Exports    5.80	 5.80	 7.68	7.68</p>
<p>U-Based on Census Bureau data. F-Includes imports.  </p>
<p>	  COTTON --------------- 1996/97		   1995/96</p>
<p>			 11/01/96  10/01/96    11/01/96  10/01/96</p>
<p> Mln Acres Planted    14.24     14.24	 16.93     16.93</p>
<p> Mln Acres Harvested  12.78     12.98	 16.01     16.01</p>
<p> Yield (Lbs per Acre)   698	 673	   537	 661</p>
<p>Note--Cotton marketing season begins Aug 1.  </p>
<p>	  COTTON-X ------------- 1996/97	     1995/96</p>
<p>			    11/01/96  10/01/96   11/01/96 10/01/96</p>
<p>	     Total Use     16.80     16.80	18.28    18.28</p>
<p>	 Unaccounted-V	 Nil	 Nil	 0.07     0.07</p>
<p>	Ending Stocks-W     4.90	4.50	 2.61     2.61</p>
<p> Avg.Price (Cents/Lb)    72.00-Z     N/A	75.40    76.90</p>
<p>V-Mln 480-lb bales. W-Difference between end stocks and prior season stocks, less total use. U-Based on Census Bureau data. N/A-Not Available. Z- The 1996/97 price is a weighted average for August-September.</p>
